-- Runaway procs (deep audit, 2026-11-15): Legendary enchant procs that fired on every hit with no ability filter and
-- no internal cooldown, because Ascension keeps those rules in its own server database and the spell data has none.
-- Part 1: spell_proc rows giving the cooldown (and chance) the tooltip states, or 0.1 sec where it states none (so one hit cannot set off a chain); the enchant still triggers its own spells.
-- Part 2: spell_proc rows that only let the named ability set the enchant off (one spell family).
-- Part 3: the named abilities set the enchant off through spell_wcme_enchant_action (several families, or an
-- extra condition); the enchant's own trigger effects are replaced by the spells each row casts (every listed
-- spell from the build with the multi-cast change; older builds cast the first one).
DELETE FROM `spell_proc` WHERE `SpellId` IN (965501, 84506, 965505, 965502, 965503, 84510, 965504, 84508, 965500, 84515, 84512, 984448, 1571129, 1573136, 274470, 274642, 274814, 965292, 272353, 1570395, 301000, 986003, 417701, 965337, 997056, 965421, 1570908, 272691, 953308, 965283, 1570238, 1575034, 954074, 954067, 1583831, 1568060, 965280);
DELETE FROM `spell_script_names` WHERE `spell_id` IN (1573136, 274470, 274642, 274814, 965292, 272353, 1570395, 301000, 986003, 417701, 965337, 997056, 965421, 1570908, 272691, 953308, 965283, 1570238, 1575034, 954074, 954067, 1583831, 1568060, 965280);
-- Part 4 (needs the build with patch 63): these drain or strike the target, so their cooldown is per target, plus
-- 0.1 sec shared (one proc per attack). Until that build, the shared spell_proc cooldown in part 1 applies.
